      <description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m doing my PhD in the ALMAnaCH team in Paris, on AI for historical linguistics. &lt;br&gt;
(For my previous engineering work, see my &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/clefourrier/&#34;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the moment, I&amp;rsquo;m developping &lt;a href=&#34;content_pages/software&#34;&gt;MEDeA&lt;/a&gt;, a Multiway Encoder Decoder Architecture, to try and do sound change/cognate predictions using neural networks. &lt;a href=&#34;publication/2020_comparing-statistical-and-neural-models-for-learning-sound-correspondences/&#34;&gt;Preliminary results&lt;/a&gt; are promising!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt; Keywords: NLP, RNN, Cognates, Etymology, Python &lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
